{"arm": "X2-P", "compounds": 0, "compounds_kept": 0, "diagnoses": [{"cell": 8, "cost_per_unit": "About 75 us of profiled time per parse call on average (1.39 s / 18,683). For link-bearing runs a full per-character Python bracket scan costs about 31 us self per run. On top of that, the range index re-parses every link destination a second time, because parse_link_with_end parses it again when th", "deal_round": 1, "doubling": "Linear: doubling the document doubles the runs and tokens. The per-run bracket map is linear in run length, so the total stays roughly 2x. No superlinear term shows at this input shape.", "gap": "Every link pays for a whole-run bracket map and a full link-range index, which re-parses all destinations and calls unikey for every pair, only to answer 'does this label contain a nested link?'. For ordinary labels without '[' the answer is always no. Separately there is per-token Python overhead i", "least_work": "One regex-driven pass over each run to find trigger characters. Each link destination parsed once. Each token rendered once. Nested-link detection is only needed when a link label itself contains an unescaped '['.", "library": "mistune", "run": 3, "unit_count": "18,683 inline parse calls produce 91,619 rendered tokens. 4,031 runs contain at least one link, and each of those triggers one build_closing_bracket_map over the whole run plus one link-range index build. That index build calls find_link_range_end, and through it _parse_link_href, for every bracket ", "unit_of_work": "One inline run (paragraph, list item, heading or table cell) passed through InlineParser.parse: tokenised, emphasis-finalised, then rendered token by token."}], "experiment": "ideas-x2-round", "kept": 3, "lane_views": [{"lane": "obvious", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "47f9157c"}, {"lane": "assume_less", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "47f9157c"}, {"lane": "eliminate", "served_model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "view_sha": "47f9157c"}, {"l