{"arm": "X2-P", "compounds": 0, "compounds_kept": 0, "diagnoses": [{"cell": 20, "cost_per_unit": "Profiled total is about 2.47 s, roughly 130 us per inline run or 27 us per rendered token. Per run, the time goes to a trigger-regex scan plus sc.match, emphasis splitting into per-part dicts and delimiter objects, and dynamic method dispatch. Each link-bearing run also gets a per-character bracket ", "deal_round": 2, "doubling": "Linear. The 700 sections are independent and every pass is O(length of each run), so doubling the input roughly doubles wall time. There is no superlinear term on this workload.", "gap": "Link handling does redundant work. For every paragraph that contains a link, label_contains_link builds a full closing-bracket map with a per-character Python loop. It then builds a link-range index that re-parses every link destination through find_link_range_end. parse_link then parses the same de", "least_work": "One left-to-right scan of each inline source to find token starts. Each link destination parsed once. One pass to pair emphasis delimiters. One render call per token.", "library": "mistune", "run": 3, "unit_count": "18,683 InlineParser.parse calls, which produce 91,619 rendered tokens. There are 4,031 bracket-map builds, 10,762 _parse_link_href calls and 22,558 _split_text_token calls.", "unit_of_work": "One inline run (paragraph, list item, heading or table cell) tokenised by InlineParser.parse, then each resulting token rendered by HTMLRenderer.render_token."}], "experiment": "ideas-x2-round", "kept": 1, "lane_views": [{"lane": "obvious", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "47f9157c"}, {"lane": "assume_less", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "47f9157c"}, {"lane": "eliminate", "served_model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "view_sha": "47f9157c"}, {"lane": "far", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "47f9157c"}, {"lane": "resolve_tradeoff", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "47f9157c"}, {"lane": "leap