{"arm": "X2-P", "compounds": 0, "compounds_kept": 0, "diagnoses": [{"cell": 11, "cost_per_unit": "About 1.3 us of Python self time per attempt (0.30 s / 233,596). Each attempt pays an isinstance check, a loop over ANCESTOR_EXCLUDES with str.lower, a getCompiledRegExp method call, creation of a finditer iterator and tuple packing and unpacking, even when the C regex finds nothing.", "deal_round": 1, "doubling": "Linear: twice as many sections gives twice as many text nodes and twice as many attempts, so wall time roughly doubles. The per-match string splice is O(len(text)), but texts are short paragraphs, so the growth stays linear.", "gap": "For the roughly 90 % of attempts that do not match, a full Python method call and its setup run around a regex search that returns None. That framing makes up most of the 16 % self share of __applyPattern, plus part of the __handleInline self time.", "least_work": "One C-level regex search per pattern per text. Python-level handling (handleMatch, stashing, string splice) is needed only for the few attempts that actually match.", "library": "markdown", "run": 3, "unit_count": "233,596 __applyPattern calls for 20,392 __handleInline calls. That is about 11.5 pattern attempts per text, and most of them end in no match (getLink, for example, runs only 3,834 times).", "unit_of_work": "One attempt of one inline pattern on one text string: a call of InlineProcessor.__applyPattern made from the __handleInline loop."}], "experiment": "ideas-x2-round", "kept": 2, "lane_views": [{"lane": "obvious", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "7b31d935"}, {"lane": "assume_less", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "7b31d935"}, {"lane": "eliminate", "served_model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "view_sha": "7b31d935"}, {"lane": "far", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "7b31d935"}, {"lane": "name_the_problem", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "7b31d935"}, {"lane": "leap", "served_model": "claude-opus-5-5"